# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtual environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
mlops_env/
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data
#
# Data NEVER goes into Git. Git is built for small text files that change line
# by line; it stores a full copy of every version of every binary file, so a
# repo with datasets in it becomes enormous and slow forever (you cannot easily
# undo it). DVC versions the data instead: the files live in DVC's storage, and
# Git gets only small POINTER files (*.dvc) holding each dataset's fingerprint.
#
# So: hide everything INSIDE data/, except the pointer files.
#   /data/?*        hide the contents of data/ (not the folder itself -- Git
#                   cannot un-hide a file inside a folder hidden as a whole)
#   !/data/*.dvc    ...but show the pointer files, which must be committed
#
# Why "?*" and not "*": "*" can match NOTHING, so "/data/*" also matches the
# folder path "data/" itself. DVC asks "is data/ ignored?" (with the slash)
# when searching for pointer files, got "yes", and never looked inside -- so
# `dvc push` silently pushed nothing. "?*" means "at least one character", so
# only things inside data/ match, never the folder itself.
#
# NOTE the leading slash: it anchors the pattern to the repository root.
# Without it, "data" would match a directory at ANY depth -- including our
# src/data/ Python package, which would then be silently excluded from every
# commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/data/?*
!/data/*.dvc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notebooks & editors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trained models
#
# Saved models are OUTPUTS of training, rebuilt from code + data at any time.
# Like data, they do not belong in Git (a forest file is tens of MB). They live
# in the MLflow model registry; nothing in the project writes models/ any more.
# Kept as a safety net in case a model is ever saved locally by hand.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/models/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local MLflow storage -- a safety net
#
# Runs belong on the MLflow server in Docker (compose.yaml). But if MLflow is
# ever used without a server address, it falls back to writing a local
# mlflow.db file or mlruns/ folder in whatever directory you are in. Those are
# run history and model files, never source code.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
mlflow.db
mlruns/
